# Frontend ↔ Quantia API

## 0. Context

Quantia manages research projects of the INNOVATEK'S / GITEMOS seedbed. This frontend (Next.js on Vercel)
consumes a closed and hardened NestJS API on Railway (F0–F7, S1–S6, P0–P6, Chat General, tech-debt backlog).

- The API is the ONLY component that talks to Postgres (Supabase), Redis, Notion and Supabase Storage.
  The frontend NEVER uses the Supabase SDK, the Notion API or Redis.
- Postgres is the system of record. Notion is a capture layer synced in the background (hence `syncStatus`).
- Budget lives ONLY in Postgres (never in Notion).
- Slow work (Notion sync, PDF, Excel) runs in a BullMQ worker: the UI shows asynchronous states.
- Real time: one Socket.io gateway with namespaces `/projects`, `/notifications` and `/general`.

Sources of truth, in this order:
1. `@quantia/contracts` v0.8.0: TS types + Zod schemas (enums, requests, responses, event payloads, exposed headers).
2. `openapi/openapi.json` in the API repo. Swagger UI (`/api/docs`) exists ONLY locally; staging and production do
   not expose it. Paths in the exported JSON do not include the `/api/v1` prefix.
3. Design System page (DS): decides HOW states, events and roles are SHOWN. The DS endpoint and payload
   inventories (§3.2, §3.3) are "proposed": when they differ from the contract, the contract wins.

If it is not in the contract, it does NOT exist: request it from the backend (§12), never simulate it in the frontend.
The UI may be STRICTER than the API (hide what the DS hides), never looser.

## 1. Environments and configuration

Operational guide (env, session, sockets, sync, reports, errors): `.cursor/docs/api-connection.md` (DS-117 / F3).

- `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL`: API origin WITHOUT suffix (e.g. `https://quantiaapi-production.up.railway.app`).
- `NEXT_PUBLIC_SOCKET_URL`: Socket.io gateway origin (usually the same host as the API).
- `src/config/env.ts` is the only module that reads `process.env` (Zod). REST calls use
  `${NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL}/api/v1`; sockets use `NEXT_PUBLIC_SOCKET_URL` + `RealtimeNamespace`.
- CORS (allowlist, `credentials: true`):
  - Production: only the production domain. Staging: also `https://*.vercel.app` (Vercel previews).
  - A non-allowed origin fails in the browser with no readable response: it is not a client bug.
- The ONLY readable response header is `Retry-After` (`HttpHeader.RETRY_AFTER` / `CORS_EXPOSED_HEADERS`).
- Healthcheck: `GET /api/v1/health` (public, Terminus `{ status: 'ok', info: { database, redis } }`).
  Use it only for a status page or a «Servicio no disponible» banner, never on every load.

## 2. Single typed HTTP client (`src/lib/api`)

- NO loose `fetch`/`axios` in components, UI hooks or server actions. Everything goes through `src/lib/api`.
- Layers (imports flow app → features → components; components never import `lib/api`):
  - `src/lib/api/client.ts`: base request (Bearer, JSON, single-flight refresh, error normalization, `Retry-After`).
  - `src/lib/api/errors.ts`: `class ApiError { statusCode; message; path; timestamp; retryAfterSeconds?: number }`.
  - `src/lib/api/{auth,users,projects,tasks,progress,documents,budget,reports,sync}.ts`: one function per endpoint
    (plus `errorUi.ts` for ErrorState mapping).
  - `src/lib/api/query-keys.ts`: cache keys per domain (`['projects', params]`, `['tasks', projectId, params]`…).
  - `src/features/<domain>/hooks`: the only place that wraps endpoint functions with the query cache.
  - `src/features/<domain>/services`: optional composition of several endpoint functions; never calls `client.ts`.
- Request, response and query types ALWAYS come from `@quantia/contracts`. Never redeclare interfaces.
- In development, validate responses with the contract Zod schema to detect drift.
- Forms validate with the contract schema (`createTaskRequestSchema`, etc.) through the DS form components.
- The API uses `whitelist + forbidNonWhitelisted`: an extra field in body or query → 400.
  Never send properties outside the contract (no `id`, `createdAt`, `syncStatus`).
- Body limits: JSON ≤ 1 MB and depth ≤ 10 (more → 400 "JSON body exceeds maximum depth").

### Data types and formats

| Data | Wire format | Display (always via `src/lib/format`) |
| --- | --- | --- |
| IDs | UUID v4 string | never shown to users |
| Date-time | ISO 8601 UTC (`2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z`) | `formatDate(v, { withTime: true })` → `09/10/2026 12:00`, America/Bogota |
| Date-only (`dueDate`, `startDate`, `endDate`) | ISO built from America/Bogota 00:00 via `toApiDate()` | `formatDate(v)` → `DD/MM/AAAA` |
| Money | decimal string `^\d+(\.\d{1,2})?$` (`"1500000.00"`) | `formatCOP(v)` → `$ 1.500.000` |
| Percent | number 0–100 (`executedPercent`, `alertThresholdPercent`) | `formatPercent(v)` → `45,6 %` |
| Nullable | arrives as `null`, never omitted | DS empty value «Sin definir» |

- Money is NEVER converted to `number` to send or to add. `formatCOP` accepts the decimal string; it may parse only to
  display. Default currency: `COP`.
- Never `new Date('YYYY-MM-DD')` for date-only fields (parses as UTC and shows the previous day in Bogotá).
- No `Intl.*`, `toLocaleString` or ad-hoc formatting outside `src/lib/format`.

### Normalized error (every 4xx/5xx)

~~~json
{ "statusCode": 403, "message": "No access to this project", "path": "/api/v1/projects/…", "timestamp": "2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z" }
~~~

- `message` is a string (multiple validation errors arrive joined). It is for logs or secondary detail; the UI ALWAYS
  decides by `statusCode` and shows DS copy (§5), never raw `message` in English.
- Never show `path`. 5xx have no technical details and the UI does not invent them.
- On 429 the client reads `response.headers.get('Retry-After')` (integer seconds) into `ApiError.retryAfterSeconds`.

### Pagination (every list except chat)

~~~ts
// Query: page (default 1), pageSize (default 20, REAL MAX 50), sortOrder 'asc' | 'desc' (default 'desc')
type Paginated<T> = { data: T[]; meta: { page: number; pageSize: number; total: number; totalPages: number } };
~~~

- The API rejects `pageSize > 50` with 400. Contract `list*QuerySchema` still allow 100 (known debt): the frontend
  ALWAYS clamps to 50 (`Math.min(pageSize, 50)`). Never try to "fetch everything".

### Mutations and cache

- Optimistic updates ONLY for task status/priority/assignee (DS: "optimista controlado") and chat messages (§6).
  On error: revert, keep the user's input and show `Toast` error. Everything else is pessimistic with `Button loading`.
- Destructive actions (delete project, task, progress, document, user, member) require `ConfirmDialog`.
- Invalidation after mutations and events:

| Trigger | Invalidate |
| --- | --- |
| task create/update/delete, `tarea.actualizada` | `['tasks', projectId]`, task detail, `['my-tasks']` |
| progress create/update/delete, `avance.registrado` | `['progress', projectId]` |
| project update, members change, `proyecto.retrasado` | `['projects']`, project detail |
| budget create/update, execution created, `presupuesto.ejecucion-baja` | `['budget', projectId]`, `['budget-executions', projectId]` |
| document upload/delete | `['documents', projectId]` |
| logout | the whole cache |

## 3. Endpoint reference

Conventions:
- Paths are relative to `/api/v1`. All require `Authorization: Bearer <accessToken>` except those marked PUBLIC.
- Common errors on any authenticated route: 401, 403 (role or membership), 404, 400 (validation or invalid UUID in
  path), 429, 500.
- "Project access" = ADMIN, the project coordinator or a member. "Project manager" = ADMIN or THE project coordinator.
- Non-existent project id → 404. Existing project without access → 403.

### 3.1 Auth (dedicated rate limit: 10 req/min per client)

**POST /auth/login** — PUBLIC
- Body `LoginRequest`: `{ email: string(email), password: string(min 8) }`
- 200 `AuthTokensResponse`: `{ accessToken, refreshToken, tokenType: 'Bearer', expiresIn }` (seconds, ≈ 900)
- 401 "Invalid credentials" (same for unknown or inactive users): one generic copy «Correo o contraseña incorrectos».
- 429 progressive lockout per email+IP: 5 failures → 60 s, 10 → 5 min, 20 → 15 min (15-min window), with
  `Retry-After`: «Demasiados intentos. Vuelve a intentarlo en Xs» with countdown; submit disabled until 0.

**POST /auth/refresh** — PUBLIC
- Body `{ refreshToken }` → 200 with a NEW refresh; the previous one is revoked (rotation).
- 401 "Invalid refresh token" · "Refresh token expired" · "User inactive" · "Refresh token reuse detected".
- Reuse revokes the WHOLE token family (logs out every device of that family).
- Two concurrent refreshes with the same token: one wins, the other gets 401 → refresh is single-flight (§4).

**POST /auth/logout** — PUBLIC — Body `{ refreshToken }` → 204 (idempotent).

### 3.2 Users

**GET /users/me** — any role → `UserResponse { id, email, fullName, isActive, roles: RoleName[], createdAt, updatedAt }`.
Source of truth for the current role and id. Never decode the JWT to read roles.

**GET /users/directory** — ADMINISTRADOR and COORDINADOR (INVESTIGADOR → 403)
- Used by the project member picker and the coordinator picker (admin).
- Query: `q` (REQUIRED, 2–100 chars after trim, matches `fullName` or `email`, case-insensitive), `page`,
  `pageSize` (≤ 50). No other params.
- 200 `{ data: UserDirectoryEntry[], meta }`, `UserDirectoryEntry = { id, fullName, email }`. Only ACTIVE users,
  ordered by `fullName`. No roles, status or dates: never infer a role from here.
- 400 when `q` is missing or < 2 chars, `pageSize > 50` or unknown params.
- UI: DS `SearchField` combobox, debounce ~300 ms, no call before 2 chars («Escribe al menos 2 caracteres»),
  `EmptyState` «Sin coincidencias», mark users already in `project.memberIds`.

ADMINISTRADOR only (others → 403):
- **GET /users?page&pageSize&sortOrder** → `PaginatedUsersResponse` (no search or role filters; search uses the directory).
- **GET /users/:id** → `UserResponse` or 404.
- **POST /users** — `{ email, password(min 8), fullName(1–200), roles: RoleName[] (min 1), isActive? }` → 201 or
  409 "Email already registered".
- **PATCH /users/:id** — partial, same rules → 200, 404, 409.
- **DELETE /users/:id** → 204 or 404. Hard delete: prefer «Desactivar» (`PATCH isActive=false`); deleting needs a
  strong `ConfirmDialog` (type the name).

### 3.3 Projects

`ProjectResponse`: `{ id, title, description, objectives, status, startDate, endDate, coordinatorId, createdById,<br>memberIds: uuid[], syncStatus, createdAt, updatedAt }` (`description`, `objectives`, `startDate`, `endDate` nullable).
`ProjectStatus`: `FORMULATION · ACTIVE · DELAYED · COMPLETED · CANCELLED`.

- **GET /projects** — any role; returns ONLY accessible projects (ADMIN all; COORDINADOR coordinated + member;
  INVESTIGADOR member). Query: `page, pageSize, status?, q? (title), sortBy: createdAt|title|status, sortOrder`.
- **GET /projects/:id** → `ProjectResponse`, 403 or 404.
- **POST /projects** — ADMINISTRADOR, COORDINADOR. Body: `{ title(1–300), description?(≤5000), objectives?(≤5000),<br>  status?, startDate?, endDate?, coordinatorId?, memberIds? }`.
  - A coordinator is always the coordinator (another `coordinatorId` → 403). An ADMIN may assign any coordinator;
    if omitted, the admin is the coordinator. Pickers use `GET /users/directory`.
  - 201 with `syncStatus: PENDING`, or 404 "Coordinator not found" / "Member user not found: …".
- **PATCH /projects/:id** — project manager. Partial body; `null` clears `startDate`/`endDate`.
  `memberIds` REPLACES the whole list: for single changes use the member endpoints. A coordinator cannot reassign
  the coordinator → 403. Status `DELAYED` emits `proyecto.retrasado`.
- **DELETE /projects/:id** — manager → 204 (hard delete; `ConfirmDialog`).
- **POST /projects/:id/members** — manager — `{ userId }` → 201, 404 "User not found", 409 "User is already a project member".
- **DELETE /projects/:id/members/:userId** — manager → 204 or 404 "Project member not found".

### 3.4 Tasks — `/projects/:projectId/tasks`

`TaskResponse`: `{ id, projectId, title, description, assigneeId, status, priority, dueDate, syncStatus, createdAt,<br>updatedAt }`. `TaskStatus`: `TODO · IN_PROGRESS · BLOCKED · DONE`. `TaskPriority`: `LOW · MEDIUM · HIGH`.
The DS inventory says `PATCH /api/v1/tasks/:id`: the real path is nested (contract wins).

- **GET** — project access. Query: `page, pageSize, status?, priority?, assigneeId?, sortBy: dueDate|priority|createdAt, sortOrder`.
- **GET /:taskId** → `TaskResponse` or 404.
- **POST** — project access (UI restricts it, §7). Body `{ title(1–300), description?(≤5000), assigneeId?, status?,<br>  priority?, dueDate? }`. `assigneeId` must be a member or the coordinator (else 403 "Assignee must be a project
  member"): the assignee picker offers ONLY `memberIds` + `coordinatorId` (never the directory).
  201 + `tarea.actualizada` + Notion sync (`PENDING`).
- **PATCH /:taskId** — assignee or manager → 200, 403, 404 (optimistic, §2).
- **DELETE /:taskId** — assignee or manager → 204, 403, 404.

### 3.5 Progress — `/projects/:projectId/progress`

`ProgressResponse`: `{ id, projectId, taskId, authorId, title, description, evidenceLinks: string[], recordedAt,<br>syncStatus, createdAt, updatedAt }` (`taskId` nullable).

- **GET** — Query: `page, pageSize, taskId?, authorId?, sortBy: recordedAt|createdAt, sortOrder`.
- **GET /:progressId** → `ProgressResponse` or 404.
- **POST** — project access. Body `{ title(1–300), description(1–10000), taskId?, evidenceLinks?: url[] (max 20),<br>  recordedAt? }`. `taskId` from another project → 400 "Task does not belong to this project".
  201 + `avance.registrado` + Notion sync. DS states: «Guardado» → `SyncStatus` pending → synced or failed.
- **PATCH / DELETE /:progressId** — author or manager → 200/204, 403, 404.

### 3.6 Documents — `/projects/:projectId/documents`

`DocumentResponse`: `{ id, projectId, uploadedById, originalName, mimeType, sizeBytes, status, createdAt }`.
`DocumentStatus`: `UPLOADED · SCANNED · QUARANTINED`.

- **POST** — project access — `multipart/form-data` with field `file` (exactly that name).
  - Allowed (real content is checked, not the extension): PDF, PNG, JPEG, XLSX. Max 25 MB (26 214 400 bytes) → 413.
  - Validate type and size in `FileUploader` BEFORE uploading; still handle 400 and 413. No file → 400 "File is required".
  - Never set `Content-Type` manually (the browser adds the `FormData` boundary).
  - Upload progress (DS "progreso de carga") uses `XMLHttpRequest.upload.onprogress` INSIDE `src/lib/api/documents.ts`
    (the only allowed non-`fetch` transport).
- **GET** — `page, pageSize, sortOrder`.
- **GET /:documentId/download** → `{ documentId, url, expiresInSeconds }` (≈ 300 s). Request it on click and open it
  immediately. NEVER store, cache, put in a static `href` or share it.
- **DELETE /:documentId** — manager → 204.

### 3.7 Budget — `/projects/:projectId/budget` (Postgres only, no `syncStatus`)

`BudgetResponse`: `{ id, projectId, totalAmount, currency, alertThresholdPercent, executedAmount, executedPercent,<br>items: BudgetItem[], createdAt, updatedAt }`. `BudgetItem`: `{ id, category, plannedAmount, notes }`.
`BudgetExecution`: `{ id, itemId, kind, amount, occurredAt, registeredById, note, createdAt }`.
`BudgetExecutionKind`: `COMMITMENT · PAYMENT · ADJUSTMENT`.

- **GET** — project access (UI shows it only if `canViewBudgetDetail`, §7).
  404 "Budget not found" = no budget YET → `EmptyState` «Sin presupuesto» (CTA «Crear presupuesto» only for
  `canManageBudget`). NOT an error screen.
- **POST** — ADMIN/COORDINADOR + manager. `{ totalAmount, currency? (default COP), alertThresholdPercent? (0–100,<br>  default 80), items?: { category(1–200), plannedAmount, notes?(≤2000) }[] (max 100) }` → 201 or 409 "Budget already exists".
- **PATCH** — same permission. `items`, if sent, REPLACES all items → 200 or 404.
- **POST /executions** — same permission. `{ itemId?, kind, amount, occurredAt?, note?(≤2000) }` → 201 or 404
  "Budget item not found". If `executedPercent < alertThresholdPercent` the API emits `presupuesto.ejecucion-baja`
  to the project room and to the coordinator's `/notifications`.
- **GET /executions** — `page, pageSize, sortOrder`.
- Rendered with DS `BudgetPanel` + `DataTable`; amounts with `formatCOP`, percentages with `formatPercent`.

### 3.8 Reports — `/projects/:projectId/reports` (dedicated limit: 5 POST/min)

- **POST** — project access. `{ kind: 'BUDGET_PDF' | 'BUDGET_EXCEL' | 'PROGRESS_PDF' }` → 201
  `{ reportId, status: 'QUEUED' }` or 429 with `Retry-After`. UI offers `BUDGET_*` only if `canViewBudgetDetail`.
- **GET /:reportId** → `{ id, projectId, requestedById, kind, status, errorMessage, downloadUrl, expiresInSeconds,<br>  createdAt, updatedAt }`. `ReportStatus`: `QUEUED → PROCESSING → READY · FAILED` (worker retries 3× with backoff).
- No list endpoint and no `reporte.completado` event in the contract: follow-up is polling (§5).

### 3.9 Chat General — `/chat/general` (can be disabled by config)

**Contracts 0.8.0 (Chat General v2).** `GeneralChatMessageDto`: `{ id, seq, version, content, clientMessageId,
createdAt, updatedAt, editedAt, deletedAt, author: PresenceUser, replyTo, reactions }`. Order by `seq`, merge by
`version`, swap optimistic bubbles by `clientMessageId`. Avatar is mandatory (`GET /users/avatars`,
`PATCH /users/me/avatar`; `403 AVATAR_REQUIRED` until chosen). Also: `GET /state`, `GET /updates?since|cursor`,
`PATCH|DELETE /messages/:id`, `PUT|DELETE /messages/:id/reaction`, `PUT /read`. Decide by `statusCode` + `code`.
Canonical integration guide: `Quantia_API/docs/development/chat-e2e-integration.md`; frontend implementation in
`.cursor/docs/api-connection.md` (Chat General v2). The v1 notes below remain valid for history/send.

- **GET /messages?cursor&limit** → `{ items, nextCursor, hasMore }`. `limit` default 30, max 100. Order: NEWEST
  FIRST, stable by `createdAt + id`; the UI reverses it to paint. Older pages: `cursor = nextCursor` while `hasMore`.
  Invalid cursor → 400. Merge pages and live events deduplicated by `id`.
- **POST /messages** — `{ content (trim, 1–2000 by config; 4000 absolute contract cap), clientMessageId? (1–64, UUID<br>  generated by the client) }` → 201 `{ message }` if created; 200 `{ message }` if that `clientMessageId` already
  existed (idempotent retry). The message is confirmed ONLY after the API persists it.
- Rate limit 20 messages/min per user → 429 with `Retry-After`: disable the composer and show the countdown.
- Disabled → REST 404 "Chat General is not enabled" and immediate socket disconnect: hide the whole section.

### 3.10 Rate limits

| Limiter | Scope | Default limit | 429 |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `default` | all routes | 120 req/min | `Retry-After` |
| `auth` | `/auth/*` | 10 req/min | `Retry-After` |
| login lockout | email + IP | 5/10/20 failures → 60 s/5 min/15 min | `Retry-After` (remaining) |
| `reports` | `POST /reports` | 5 req/min | `Retry-After` |
| `chat-general` | `POST /chat/general/messages` | 20 req/min per user | `Retry-After` |

`/health` has no limit. Every 429 carries `Retry-After` in integer seconds, readable through CORS.

## 4. Authentication and session

- Access JWT: 15 min. Refresh: 7 days, rotating, revocable, with reuse detection.
- `accessToken` → ONLY in memory (auth store). Never in `localStorage`/`sessionStorage`/readable cookies.
  On reload it is recovered through refresh.
- `refreshToken` → `httpOnly; Secure; SameSite=Strict; Path=/api/session` cookie set by minimal Next route handlers
  (`src/app/api/session/{login,refresh,logout}/route.ts`) that forward to the API and NEVER return the refresh to
  browser JS (only `accessToken` and `expiresIn`). Reason: the API returns the refresh in the body, and a 7-day token
  readable by JS is the most valuable asset under XSS.
- Those handlers are the only exception to direct access and belong to the session transport of `src/lib/api`. They:
  forward the API status and `Retry-After` as is (login 429 needs it), reject requests whose `Origin` is not the app
  origin (CSRF), and respond with `Cache-Control: no-store`.
- Boot: `session/refresh` → 200: `GET /users/me` → hydrate role → redirect to the role landing (§8); 401 → `/login`.
  While booting, the shell shows `Skeleton` of `RoleSidebar` + `AppHeader` (DS "skeleton de navegación").
- Refresh: proactive ~60 s before `expiresIn`; reactive on any 401 (except auth routes) with ONE refresh in flight
  (single-flight), concurrent requests wait and retry ONCE. Refresh fails → session-expired modal (§5). Never loop.
- Tabs: `BroadcastChannel('quantia-auth')` so only one tab rotates the refresh and the others receive the new access
  token (otherwise reuse detection would close the session).
- After every refresh: revalidate `/users/me` (deactivated user or changed roles) and update `socket.auth.token`.
- Logout: `session/logout` → API revokes → clear cookie, store and query cache, disconnect ALL sockets, clear session
  drafts and pending report ids, notify other tabs.

## 5. Mandatory state map (DS §4.5)

Every screen or component that consumes data renders these states with REGISTERED DS components only
(`EmptyState`, `Skeleton`, `ErrorState`, `ConfirmDialog`, `Toast`, `SyncStatus`, `ConnectionStatus`).
No generic spinner, no blank screen.

| Situation | DS component | Copy (es-CO) and behaviour |
| --- | --- | --- |
| First load | `Skeleton` shaped like the final content | does not block global navigation |
| Refetch with data | keep data + subtle indicator | never back to `Skeleton` |
| Empty list (`meta.total === 0`, no filters) | `EmptyState` | specific message + next action; CTA only if the role can create |
| Empty by filters/search | `EmptyState` | «Sin resultados» + «Limpiar filtros» |
| Budget 404 | `EmptyState` | «Sin presupuesto» (+ CTA for managers) |
| Directory `q` < 2 chars | field help text | «Escribe al menos 2 caracteres» (no API call) |
| 400 | inline field errors | message next to the field; never only a toast |
| 401 after refresh fails | session-expired dialog | «Tu sesión expiró» without unmounting the screen; keep the form draft (sessionStorage, NO tokens) and retry the action after re-login |
| 403 | `ErrorState` forbidden | «No tienes permiso» + «Volver a [landing]»; never reveal whether the resource exists; no silent redirect |
| 404 | `ErrorState` not-found | «No encontrado» + back action |
| 409 | inline or `Toast` | concrete conflict (email duplicado, ya es miembro, presupuesto existente) + refetch |
| 413 | `FileUploader` error | «El archivo supera 25 MB» |
| 429 | `ErrorState` rate-limit (inline in forms) | «Estamos procesando demasiadas solicitudes. Reintentando en Xs» with visible countdown from `Retry-After`; source action disabled |
| 5xx / offline | `ErrorState` server | recoverable error + «Reintentar», no technical details |
| WebSocket down | `ConnectionStatus` | «Datos posiblemente desactualizados» + auto reconnect + «Reconectar» (F-04) |

429 rules:
- Never retry before `Retry-After` expires. At most ONE automatic retry after the wait (DS "reintento automático con
  espera visible"); after that, manual only. Missing header (proxy): local fallback 5 s → 10 s → 30 s.
- Countdown text updates visually every second but is announced only at start and end (polite live region).
- `RateLimitNotice` is NOT in the DS inventory: implement it as `ErrorState variant="rate-limit"` fed by
  `ApiError.retryAfterSeconds` until it is registered in Figma and the DS.

### Notion sync — `SyncStatus`

Applies to projects, tasks and progress (`syncStatus: PENDING · SYNCED · FAILED`):
- `PENDING` → badge «Sincronizando con Notion»; the user keeps working.
- `FAILED` → banner «No se pudo sincronizar con Notion». The Quantia data IS valid: never block reading or editing.
  Only ADMINISTRADOR sees «Reintentar» (F-05 / DS-120) via provisional `POST /sync/:entityType/:id/retry`
  (`src/lib/api/sync.ts`). Response schemas are still pending in `@quantia/contracts` (§12); do not invent
  a `sync.failed` socket event.
- `SYNCED` → no indicator (or a discreet check).
- Scope (DS): Investigador sees the state of his own data, Coordinador of his portfolio, Admin everything.
- `syncStatus` is NOT in socket payloads: after an event, refetch the resource.
- Budget, documents, reports, directory and chat have no `syncStatus`.

### Async jobs — reports («Generando reporte»)

1. `POST /reports` → store `{ reportId, kind, projectId }` in a GLOBAL reports store (in memory + sessionStorage,
   no URLs) so polling survives navigation (DS: "continuar navegando y recibir notificación").
2. Poll `GET /reports/:reportId` with backoff 2 s → 4 s → 8 s (cap 30 s; stop after ~5 min → «Revisar más tarde»).
3. `READY` → `Toast` «Reporte listo» with action «Descargar» (`downloadUrl`; if `expiresInSeconds` passed, GET again).
4. `FAILED` → «No se pudo generar el reporte» + «Reintentar» (new POST). Never show raw `errorMessage`.
5. Disable «Generar» while a report of the same `kind` is running in that project, or while a `Retry-After` runs.

### Documents — status

- `UPLOADED` → «En revisión» (no download until `SCANNED`). `SCANNED` → downloadable.
- `QUARANTINED` → «Bloqueado por seguridad», no download action.

## 6. Real time (Socket.io)

- A single provider in `src/lib/socket/` (`connection.ts`, `events.ts`, `SocketProvider.tsx`,
  `useProjectSocket.ts`) owns every socket. NO sockets in components; components subscribe through hooks.
- Server limits: 5 simultaneous connections per user (ALL tabs and namespaces), 30 events/s per socket, 60 s idle
  (covered by Socket.io ping/pong). Exceeding → `error { message: 'Too many connections' }` + disconnect.
- Connection budget (one tab with all three namespaces already uses 3 of 5):
  - `/notifications`: while signed in.
  - `/projects`: only while a project view is mounted.
  - `/general`: only while the Chat General view is mounted.
  - "Too many connections" → no reconnect loop; `ConnectionStatus` «Tiempo real pausado en esta pestaña» and the
    view keeps working with REST (refetch on focus).
- Connect: `io(socketUrl + ns, { auth: { token: accessToken }, transports: ['websocket'] })`. Never put the token
  in the query string.
- Token rejected → server disconnects silently: refresh once and reconnect with the new token; if it fails → session
  expired. After every refresh update `socket.auth.token` (used on the next reconnect).
- ALWAYS use `RealtimeNamespace`, `RealtimeEvent` and `ChatGeneralEvent` from `@quantia/contracts`.
- Validate every payload with its Zod schema (`tareaActualizadaPayloadSchema.safeParse`…); drop invalid ones.
- Events INVALIDATE or patch the cache; they are not the source of truth. After reconnect → refetch the active view.
- Disconnect → `ConnectionStatus` «Datos posiblemente desactualizados» (no blocking), Socket.io auto-reconnect with
  backoff and a manual «Reconectar» button; on reconnect hide the banner, re-join and refetch.
- No listening to or emitting events outside the contract.

### `/projects`

- On connect the server emits `authenticated { userId }`.
- Client → `join { projectId }` with ack `{ ok: true, room }` or `{ ok: false, error }`. The server checks
  membership. Join when entering a project view and again after every reconnect. `ok: false` → do not retry; REST keeps working.
- There is no `leave`: ignore events whose `payload.projectId` is not the active project.

### Event → cache → visual response (DS §3.2, §4.5, D-07)

| Event (contract payload) | Cache | Visual response | Who sees it |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `tarea.actualizada` `{ projectId, taskId, title, status, priority, assigneeId, updatedAt }` | patch the cached row, refetch detail (sync state) | update the `TaskRow` IN PLACE + 1–2 s highlight; never reorder under the cursor or focus | project view members |
| `avance.registrado` `{ projectId, progressId, taskId, title, authorId, recordedAt, updatedAt }` | invalidate progress | insert into `ActivityTimeline` without moving focus; if scrolled, pill «N avances nuevos» | project view members |
| `proyecto.retrasado` `{ projectId, title, status: 'DELAYED', endDate, updatedAt }` | invalidate project | status `Badge` «Retrasado» for everyone; persistent `AlertList` item only if `canManageProject` | badge: all; alert: managers |
| `presupuesto.ejecucion-baja` `{ projectId, budgetId, executedPercent, thresholdPercent, updatedAt }` | invalidate budget | alert card «Ejecución baja: 45,6 % de 80 %» + «Ver presupuesto» | only `canViewBudgetDetail` |

- D-07: when a patch would change the order of a sorted list, keep the visible order and show «Lista actualizada ·
  Reordenar»; the new order applies on user action, page or filter change.
- Highlights respect `prefers-reduced-motion` (static outline instead of animation).
- Announce through the single polite live region (accessibility-ux), max one announcement per burst.
- The DS proposes extra payload fields (`dueDate`, `summary`, `reason`, `severity`, `progressPercent`): they are not
  in the contract; do not read them (§12).

### `/notifications`

- Automatic personal room (`user:<id>`), no join.
- `presupuesto.ejecucion-baja` reaches the coordinator here AND through `/projects`: deduplicate by
  `projectId + updatedAt` before showing anything.
- No REST for notifications: they are ephemeral (`Toast` + in-memory notification center for the session).

### `/general` (Chat General)

- JWT required; after validation the server joins the socket to the fixed room `general` automatically (no `join`).
- v2 (contracts 0.8.0) adds `usuario-actualizado`, `mensaje-editado`, `mensaje-eliminado`, `reacciones-actualizadas`,
  `escribiendo`, `lectura` and `error { code }`; client → server `escribiendo { isTyping }` and
  `reautenticar { token }` (ack). Ready only after `presencia`; after a reconnect, catch up with `/updates`.
- `chat.general.presencia { users: PresenceUser[], typing, generatedAt, tokenExpiresAt }` → REPLACE the presence list (also after reconnect).
- `chat.general.usuario-conectado { user, occurredAt }` / `chat.general.usuario-desconectado { userId, occurredAt }`
  → upsert/remove in a `Map` keyed by `userId`. Several tabs of one user count as ONE presence and "disconnected" only
  arrives when the last socket closes: never infer offline from your own tab closing.
- `PresenceUser` exposes only `id`, `name`, `avatar` (`AVATAR_01…05`), `avatarUrl` (always `null`): no emails or roles in the chat UI.
- `chat.general.mensaje-creado { message }` → append if its `id` or `clientMessageId` is not already present.
- Send ALWAYS via REST, never by socket. Optimistic message states:
  - `sending` (generated `clientMessageId`, muted style) → `sent` on 201/200 or the matching `mensaje-creado`.
  - `failed` → «No se envió · Reintentar»; retry with the SAME `clientMessageId` (the API answers 200, no duplicates).
- Scroll: new messages do not move the view if the user scrolled up; show pill «Nuevos mensajes». Older history loads
  at the top keeping the scroll anchor.
- Message list `role="log"`; content rendered as plain text (`white-space: pre-wrap`), counter «X/2000», send
  disabled when empty, sending or during 429.
- Immediate disconnect on connect = chat disabled → hide the section and its navigation entry.

## 7. Authorization in the UI

The API decides (deny by default + object-level authorization). The UI only HIDES what does not apply (it may be
stricter than the API, following the DS matrix) and ALWAYS handles 403 as the safety net.

Required helpers in `src/lib/auth/permissions.ts`, computed from `/users/me` and the resource:

| Helper | Rule |
| --- | --- |
| `primaryRole(me)` | highest privilege: ADMINISTRADOR > COORDINADOR > INVESTIGADOR |
| `isAdmin(me)`, `isCoordinator(me)` | role check |
| `canSearchUsers(me)` | admin or coordinator |
| `canManageUsers(me)` | admin |
| `canManageProject(me, project)` | admin or `project.coordinatorId === me.id` |
| `canManageMembers(me, project)` | `canManageProject` (uses `/users/directory`) |
| `canCreateTask(me, project)` | `canManageProject` (DS: Investigador does not create tasks; API allows it) |
| `canEditTask(me, project, task)` | `canManageProject` or `task.assigneeId === me.id` |
| `canCreateProgress(me, project)` | project access |
| `canEditProgress(me, project, p)` | `canManageProject` or `p.authorId === me.id` |
| `canDeleteDocument(me, project)` | `canManageProject` |
| `canViewBudgetDetail(me)` | admin or coordinator (DS: Investigador «sin detalle financiero») |
| `canManageBudget(me, project)` | (admin or coordinator) and `canManageProject` |
| `canGenerateReport(me, kind)` | `PROGRESS_PDF`, or `BUDGET_*` if `canViewBudgetDetail` |
| `canViewAudit(me)` | admin (coordinator only if approved; no endpoint yet) |
| `canRetrySync(me)` | admin (no endpoint yet) |

Never trust a `projectId` in local state to "grant" access: if the API answers 403/404, render that state.

## 8. Navigation and landing by role (DS §2.2, D-06)

Roles (`RoleName`): `INVESTIGADOR`, `COORDINADOR`, `ADMINISTRADOR`; several roles → `primaryRole`.

| Module | INVESTIGADOR | COORDINADOR | ADMINISTRADOR |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Landing | `/mis-tareas` «Mis tareas» | `/panel` group dashboard | `/institucional` institutional view |
| Projects | where member (`/mis-proyectos/[projectId]`) | portfolio (`/cartera/[projectId]`): coordinated + member, tagged | all |
| Create / edit / delete project | — | yes (he is the coordinator) / those he coordinates | yes (assigns coordinator) |
| Members (directory) | — | projects he coordinates | yes |
| Tasks | view and update assigned | create, assign, reassign, change date in portfolio | global |
| Progress | create and view in his projects | view in portfolio (comments: §12) | view all |
| Documents | view and upload; no delete | manage in portfolio | institutional |
| Budget | hidden | view and manage in portfolio (create, edit, register executions) | view and manage detail |
| Reports | `PROGRESS_PDF` of his projects | PDF/Excel of portfolio | PDF/Excel (institutional: §12) |
| Users | own profile only | — | CRUD users and roles |
| Audit | — | only if approved | full (§12) |
| Sync | state of own data | state of portfolio | state + provisional retry (DS-120; schemas §12) |
| Chat General | yes (if enabled) | yes | yes |

- Sections without permission are NOT rendered (not disabled, not greyed) and are absent from `RoleSidebar`.
- Group `layout.tsx` `RoleGate`: a role without the view is redirected to its landing. UX only; the API is the authority.

## 9. Pagination and filters in the URL (RF-19)

- Every list uses `page` and `pageSize` (default 20, max 50) and renders `meta` with DS `Pagination`.
- Filters, sort and page live in search params with the EXACT contract names (route segments are Spanish; query
  params are not):
  - Projects: `page, pageSize, status, q, sortBy(createdAt|title|status), sortOrder`
  - Tasks: `page, pageSize, status, priority, assigneeId, sortBy(dueDate|priority|createdAt), sortOrder`
  - Progress: `page, pageSize, taskId, authorId, sortBy(recordedAt|createdAt), sortOrder`
  - Documents / executions / users: `page, pageSize, sortOrder`
- The user directory lives in the combobox state, NOT in the URL. Chat General uses cursor + infinite scroll, not the URL.
- Parse with the contract `list*QuerySchema` and clamp `pageSize` to 50; invalid values fall back to the default.
  Never send empty or unknown params (400).
- Changing a filter resets `page=1`. Searches (`q`) debounce ~300 ms. `page > totalPages` after a delete → last valid page.
- Filter UI: DS `FilterBar` + `SearchField`; enum labels in Spanish come from one map per enum
  in `statusPresentation.ts` (accessibility-ux §1, e.g. `TaskStatus.IN_PROGRESS` → «En curso»), never inline strings.

## 10. Client security

- No secrets in `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` except the API URL.
- No tokens in `localStorage`, logs, analytics, URLs, error messages or session drafts.
- Never render API HTML (`dangerouslySetInnerHTML` forbidden): chat, descriptions and progress are plain text.
- `evidenceLinks`: show only `http(s)`, open with `target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"`.
- Signed URLs (documents, reports): ephemeral, never persisted.
- Directory results and emails: not cached beyond the session, never sent to analytics.
- Session route handlers: `Origin` check, `no-store`, never log bodies.

## 11. Definition of Done per screen

- [ ] Only `src/lib/api` functions through `features/<domain>/hooks`; zero `fetch` in components.
- [ ] Types, enums and validation 100 % from `@quantia/contracts` v0.8.0; no extra fields in requests.
- [ ] Renders the §5 map with registered DS components: `Skeleton`, `EmptyState`, 400 inline, 401 keeping the draft,
      403, 404, 409, 429 with `Retry-After` countdown, 5xx and `ConnectionStatus`.
- [ ] `SyncStatus` on projects, tasks and progress; «Generando reporte» persists across navigation; document status.
- [ ] Sockets only via the provider, within the connection budget; contract events validated with Zod; dedupe;
      re-join and refetch after reconnect.
- [ ] Live updates patch in place with a 1–2 s highlight, no reordering under the cursor, polite announcement.
- [ ] Navigation, landing and actions follow §7–§8; nothing disabled-but-visible.
- [ ] Member/coordinator pickers use `GET /users/directory` (≥ 2 chars, debounce); task assignees only from
      `memberIds` + `coordinatorId`.
- [ ] Paginated lists (`pageSize` ≤ 50) with filters and sort in the URL.
- [ ] Money as decimal string, dates ISO; all display through `formatCOP`, `formatDate`, `formatPercent`.
- [ ] Chat: optimistic states with the same `clientMessageId` on retry, dedupe by `id`, scroll anchor, plain text.
- [ ] No tokens outside memory / httpOnly cookie.

## 12. Contract gaps (do NOT simulate)

The DS requires these, but they are not in `@quantia/contracts` v0.8.0. Do not render the feature (or render the
`EmptyState` agreed with design) and open a backend issue in Linear:

| DS need | Missing in the contract | Until it exists |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Coordinator/admin KPIs (`GET /dashboard`) | dashboard endpoint | `/panel` and `/institucional` compose KPIs from `GET /projects` (status counts via `meta.total` per status filter) |
| «Mis tareas» across projects | cross-project "my tasks" endpoint | `GET /projects` + `GET /projects/:id/tasks?assigneeId=me.id` per project, max 4 concurrent, `pageSize` 50 |
| Sync retry schemas + `sync.failed` | Formal POST response / event | Provisional admin `POST /sync/:entityType/:id/retry` (DS-120); UI from REST `syncStatus`; no socket |
| `reporte.completado` | event | polling (§5 / DS-121); when added, it can stop polling and fire the `Toast` |
| Audit, convocatorias, institutional reports | endpoints | render only the «Próximamente» placeholder (`ComingSoonScreen`): no data, no fixtures, no controls |
| Comments, mentions, institutional deviation comparison | endpoints | do not render these sections at all |
| Comments on progress (Coordinador) | endpoint | read-only progress |
| Event fields `dueDate`, `summary`, `reason`, `severity`, `progressPercent` | payload fields | refetch the resource |

